### Method 2: X++ Code on Form

If you want to call the report from a method instead of a button:

```xpp
public void printCashInvoice()
{
    AVARUMCashSalesCashVoucher cashVoucher;
    Args args;
    MenuFunction menuFunction;
    
    // Get the current record from the form datasource
    cashVoucher = AVARUMCashSalesCashVoucher_ds.cursor();
    
    if (!cashVoucher.RecId)
    {
        warning("Please select a cash voucher to print.");
        return;
    }
    
    // Create Args and set the record
    args = new Args();
    args.record(cashVoucher);
    args.caller(this);
    
    // Create and run the menu function
    menuFunction = new MenuFunction(
        menuItemOutputStr(AVARUMCashInvoice),
        MenuItemType::Output
    );
    
    menuFunction.run(args);
}
```

You can call this from:
- Button clicked() event
- Form menu item
- Right-click context menu

